{
  "_comment": [
    "Which Zigbee button does what. EXAMPLE file: the real one lives in",
    "/etc/maman-tv-lite/buttons.json, outside the repository, so that updating",
    "the code never changes what a button does.",
    "",
    "scripts/setup-zigbee.py writes this file for you by watching a real",
    "button being pressed. Action names differ between models, so learning",
    "them beats guessing: single, double, hold, on, toggle, 1_single...",
    "",
    "Keys are device names as Zigbee2MQTT publishes them, on the topic",
    "zigbee2mqtt/<name>. The special key \"*\" matches any device, and a",
    "device's own entry wins over it.",
    "",
    "Commands must come from the COMMANDS whitelist in api/zigbee_bridge.py;",
    "list them with ./scripts/setup-zigbee.py --list-commands. An unknown",
    "name is logged and ignored, never executed.",
    "",
    "After editing by hand: sudo systemctl restart maman-api"
  ],
  "bindings": {
    "*": {
      "single": "power_toggle"
    },
    "living-room-button": {
      "single": "power_toggle",
      "double": "channel_up",
      "hold": "mute"
    }
  }
}
